<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="032" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Extracted invoices carry Matter field mapping: a fill-only mapping step inside InvoiceSubmissionPersister, before its transaction (FR-20; owner ruling 2026-11-06)</title>
    <phase>3 W3 Product creators onto the service</phase>
    <gate>notes/task-032-design.md reviewed by ebilling-r1 AND unified-access-control-r2, every question in its section 12 answered and recorded in notes/decisions.md. No code before both reviews.</gate>
    <status>blocked</status>
    <blocked-reason>Design review by ebilling-r1 and UAC-r2 (owner ruling 2026-11-06).</blocked-reason>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api; tags include bff-api, finance, security; the step writes into a one-transaction create with fixed ids (data-mutation) as the system principal; changes a UAC-r2 guarded ArchTest (#2188 mask guard) and adds tests at KEEP paths (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The design (notes/task-032-design.md) fixes the placement, the principal, every protected column, the fault rules and the guard; the work is a bounded new static class plus a small persister edit, executed literally. Escalate to opus if a review answer changes the design.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W3-server</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits ebilling-r1's InvoiceSubmissionPersister.cs; must rebase on work/ebilling-r1 and run /conflict-check (ebilling 095d-2b-2, 164a, 165a are nearby).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>019; design review (gate); the app-only column-metadata reader (task 052 scope, see constraint "metadata reader")</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, finance, security, field-mapping, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>10-14 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement notes/task-032-design.md exactly. Add a fill-only mapping step that `InvoiceSubmissionPersister.PersistCoreAsync` calls on the in-memory invoice entity after every persister-written column is set and immediately before `_lifecycle.BuildInvoiceCreateRequest(invoice, initial)`, so the one `ExecuteTransactionAsync` commits the invoice with the mapped values. The step reuses the field-mapping engine directly (`CreateTimeFieldMapping`, `MappingSourceReadProbe` with `MappingSourceReader.System`, the profile read on `IFieldMappingDataverseService`, `RecordCreationService.ProtectedFromMapping` / `NormalizedRule` / `IsFilingLookup` as they are) and never calls `RecordCreationService` itself. Fill-only: an extracted or persister value always wins. A mapping fault, a missing profile or an unreadable source never fails, refuses or retries the submission: it maps nothing and, for a fault, records an admin-attention note in the same transaction.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, e-billing submission persistence and field mapping. Follow ADRs strictly. The design is the contract: where it and this POML disagree, stop and ask.</role>
  <goal>A submission whose core record (matter, project or work assignment) has an active field-mapping profile to sprk_invoice produces an invoice whose unsupplied, unprotected columns are filled from that core record, in the same single transaction, with the same deterministic ids; every other submission persists exactly as today.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner ruling 2026-11-06 (notes/decisions.md "Owner rulings", 032 bullet; "W3 direction" 032 bullet): `InvoiceSubmissionPersister` stays the single creator of the invoice family; mapping is a fill-only step inside it, before its transaction, calling the same mapping engine (W3 option 2); `RecordCreationService` does not change. Design inputs from ebilling-r1: notes/task-032-design-inputs.md (conditions 1-6). Prior escalation (superseded by the ruling): notes/task-032-notes.md. The previous POML target (`InvoiceReviewService.CreateInvoiceRecordAsync`) no longer exists (ebilling-r1 050a / D-134).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionPersister.cs (ebilling-r1 owns it; work/ebilling-r1 b07e220fa6: PersistCoreAsync :300, invoice entity :461, owner :476, FillInvoice call :546, BuildInvoiceCreateRequest :614, adminAttention + submission update :708-716, ExecuteTransactionAsync :730, generic transaction catch :757, ResumeAsync :1082; re-grep)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping.cs (the step; static, no DI registration)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/AdminAttentionText.cs (only if ebilling-r1 answers design Q-E2 with option a: one new segment kind)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/MappingSourceCallerMaskGuardTests.cs (one UnmaskedCallExemptions entry, Uses = 1; KnownCallSites 3 -> 4; only with UAC-r2's answer to design Q-U3)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/InvoiceExtractionMappingGuardTests.cs (the named-exception guard, section 9 of the design)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Finance/Submission/InvoiceExtractionFieldMappingTests.cs (the step's unit tests)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionPersisterMappingTests.cs (the persister with the step: placement, fill-only, one transaction, faults)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.Repair.cs (RepairMappingAsync :253-441: the system-principal use of the same engine)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.Mapping.cs (MapFieldsAsync :255-402; ProtectedFromMapping :184; IsFilingLookup :94; NormalizedRule :1145)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/MappingSourceReadProbe.cs (ReadAsync :265; MappingSourceReader.System :47)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/CreateTimeFieldMapping.cs (CollectSourceColumns :77; ApplyFillOnly :126)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionPersisterTests.cs (on work/ebilling-r1: the persister's fakes; reuse, do not copy)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="019" status="required">W2 service deployed and reviewed.</dependency>
      <dependency task="design-review" status="required">ebilling-r1 and UAC-r2 answers to design section 12, recorded in notes/decisions.md.</dependency>
      <dependency task="052" status="shared">The app-only column-metadata reader. One reader, never two: use 052's if it has landed; otherwise add it here as 052's scope describes and 052 consumes it.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner ruling 2026-11-06">Scope: creator. `InvoiceSubmissionPersister` remains the only code that creates the invoice family on the extraction path. No new creator, no second transaction outside the persister, no call to `RecordCreationService.CreateAsync` or any other `RecordCreationService` instance member.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner ruling 2026-11-06">Scope: RecordCreationService. No change to any `RecordCreationService*.cs` file (no given-id input, no multi-row create, no system-principal mapping mode, no visibility change). Its existing `internal static` members are called as they are.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-02">Scope: precedence. Fill-only through `CreateTimeFieldMapping.ApplyFillOnly` on the invoice as the persister built it; every column the persister set is supplied and never overwritten.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design section 5">Scope: protected targets. A rule whose target is in the design's protected set (section 5: ProtectedFromMapping, RefuseAppOnlyWrite per target, the persister-owned columns written or conditionally written, the status pair, the invoice id, the firm and firm hold, the submitter columns, the supersedes link, sprk_document, the search-index columns, the access-conferring columns, every column a registered external module for sprk_invoice may read, and every filing lookup) is skipped, never written, whether or not the persister set it this time.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028; design section 4">Scope: identity. The source, the profile and the metadata are read app-only as the system principal (`MappingSourceReader.System`); no OBO, no impersonation, no caller probe. The source is only ever the submission's core record (`outcome.CoreRecord`), passed explicitly; never inferred from the invoice's columns.</constraint>
    <constraint source="#2188; design section 4.3">Scope: field security. Every source column whose metadata says IsSecured, or whose IsSecured cannot be read, removes the whole step's output (fail closed for unknown) or the column (known secured), as the design states. Never a fallback to "not secured".</constraint>
    <constraint source="design section 7">Scope: faults. Nothing in the step returns Retry, Refused, ReEvaluate or throws to the persister (cancellation of the job's own token aside). A fault maps nothing at all (no partial set) and adds the admin-attention note; a missing profile and a profile with no applicable rules map nothing silently.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ebilling-r1 (CLAUDE.md §4)">Scope: transaction. Ids stay `InvoiceIdFor` / `LineIdFor` / `ApprovalIdFor`; the request order and count of the transaction are unchanged except as the design's section 8 allows (the one mapping-free re-commit, only if ebilling-r1 answers Q-E1 with option a). Lines, approval, Stored File rows and the submission row are never mapping targets. `ResumeAsync` never maps.</constraint>
    <constraint source="metadata reader">Scope: metadata. Target type, IsValidForCreate, MaxLength, DateTimeBehavior, lookup Targets and source IsSecured come from the one app-only column-metadata reader (task 052 scope), read per delivery or from a cache no longer than the design states; a value that does not fit its target exactly as the SDK needs it is dropped, never coerced silently.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. No new registration and no new interface (ADR010_DITests ceiling unchanged). New persister constructor parameters are optional trailing parameters of already-registered services; a null one makes the step map nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Scope: logs and notes. Log lines and the admin-attention note carry codes, column names and ids only; never a mapped or extracted value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. Placement Justification in the PR; fresh-master publish-size delta; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038; testing.md:132">Scope: tests. New tests under tests/unit/domain/** and tests/Spaarke.ArchTests only; existing persister tests change only to follow a moved dependency, never by weakening an assertion; every guard ships with must-fire and must-not-fire controls.</constraint>
  </constraints>

