  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor. Confirm the gate (review answers in decisions.md). `git switch -c task/fm-032-impl` from the work branch, merge or rebase onto work/ebilling-r1, run /conflict-check. Re-grep every line the design cites.</step>
    <step order="1">Metadata reader: confirm whether 052's app-only column-metadata reader exists; if not, add it as 052's scope describes (extend MetadataService) with its own tests.</step>
    <step order="2">Write the failing tests of design section 10 first (unit and guard).</step>
    <step order="3">Add InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping (design sections 3-7) and call it from PersistCoreAsync at the design's position; thread its admin-attention note into the existing submission update.</step>
    <step order="4">Only if Q-E1 = option a: the one mapping-free re-commit (design section 8).</step>
    <step order="5">Guards: the #2188 exemption entry (with UAC-r2's answer) and InvoiceExtractionMappingGuardTests with controls.</step>
    <step order="6">Build; run the persister suites, the handler suites, MappingSourceCallerMaskGuardTests, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests, ADR010_DITests and the field-mapping unit suites; publish-size delta; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="7">Adversarial review: two passes (security). Record deviations in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/task-032-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A review answer changes the placement, the principal, the protected set or the fault rule: STOP; the design is re-issued before code.</trigger>
    <trigger>Implementing needs any change to a RecordCreationService*.cs file: STOP and escalate (owner ruling forbids it).</trigger>
    <trigger>The persister on work/ebilling-r1 has moved so that no single point after the last persister-written invoice column and before BuildInvoiceCreateRequest exists: STOP and ask ebilling-r1.</trigger>
    <trigger>The metadata reader cannot tell IsSecured for a source column on a live table: STOP; never ship with a "not secured" default.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>RecordCreationService.MapFieldsAsync (caller principal, Web API item) and RepairMappingAsync (system principal, existing row) are the two engine callers; both are private members of the service, which the ruling forbids changing or calling for this create.</existing>
    <extension>The engine itself is reused unchanged (static CreateTimeFieldMapping, MappingSourceReadProbe, the service's internal static helpers). The one new class is needed because the persister cannot reach either private caller and the ruling keeps the service closed; it holds only the invoice-specific protection and fault rules.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-20 is not met for extracted invoices: every invoice from the submission job lacks the Matter fields the profile names (owner ruling 2026-11-06 requires them in R1).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceExtractionFieldMapping.cs</output>
