  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AC1 Placement: PersistCoreAsync calls the step exactly once per non-resume persist, after FillInvoice, the creator stamp, sprk_submittedby, the supersedes link and the review detail are set, and before BuildInvoiceCreateRequest; the transaction's invoice create carries the mapped columns (unit test asserting the CreateRequest target).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC2 Fill-only: with a profile that targets a column the persister set (for example sprk_name, sprk_totalamount, sprk_invoicenumber), the committed value is the persister's (unit test per column).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC3 Mapping happens: with an active profile from the core table to sprk_invoice and a Copy rule into an unprotected, unset column, the committed invoice carries the source value; the same holds for a project and a work assignment core record (unit tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC4 Protected targets (negative, one test per column, design section 5): a rule targeting each listed column writes nothing to it, including statecode, statuscode, sprk_invoiceid, ownerid, sprk_createdbyperson, sprk_submittedby, sprk_vendororg (also when the submission has no firm), sprk_firmhold, sprk_document, the supersedes link, sprk_reviewdetail, every money total, sprk_currency, sprk_invoicedate and the billing period (also when extraction found none), every core lookup, the search-index columns, and every column of a registered sprk_invoice external module's ReadableColumns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC5 Field security (negative): a Copy from a source column the metadata marks IsSecured writes nothing for that column and the other rules still apply; a metadata read fault or an unknown IsSecured maps nothing at all and adds the note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC6 Faults never fail the submission (negative): a profile read fault, a source read fault, a metadata fault and an exception thrown inside the step each give the same persist status, reason code, ids and request count as the same submission with no profile, with no mapped column on the invoice and the note in the submission update.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC7 Silent no-ops: no profile, a profile with no rules, and a profile whose every rule is skipped map nothing and add no note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC8 Value fit (negative): a mapped value of the wrong SDK type, over MaxLength, into a column not valid for create, into a date column of unknown behaviour, or a lookup whose target table the column does not accept is dropped, and the transaction is built without it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC9 Transaction shape: ids, request order and request count are identical with and without mapping; lines, approval, Stored File rows and the submission update carry no mapped column; ResumeAsync makes no mapping read (unit test with a throwing profile reader on a resumed submission).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC10 Source: the step reads only outcome.CoreRecord's table and id; the mapping read uses MappingSourceReader.System; no caller probe and no OBO client is used (unit test with recording fakes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC11 Guard: InvoiceExtractionMappingGuardTests pins the step's call position in PersistCoreAsync, no mapping call in ResumeAsync, the invoice local as the only target, and no RecordCreationService instance member in the persister or the step; each with must-fire and must-not-fire controls. The #2188 guard passes with exactly one new exemption (Uses = 1) and KnownCallSites = 4.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC12 Unchanged: no RecordCreationService*.cs file and no InvoiceSubmissionRerunJobHandler.cs file is in the diff; existing persister, handler, MappingSourceCallerMaskGuardTests (other than the entry), RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests and ADR010_DITests pass with unchanged assertions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC13 BFF build 0 errors; publish-size delta and CVE result recorded in notes/task-032-notes.md.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Re-scoped 2026-11-07 to the owner ruling of 2026-11-06. Design: notes/task-032-design.md. Live check: task 036 (a submission under a profiled matter on dev).</notes>

